#---
# purpose: A closure over an integer or a float, applied by a helper planned once for each, is entered by the arm whose capture lane matches the value the closure holds on all three paths
# root: main/0
# assert.metric.semantic.activations: 9
# assert.metric.semantic.executables: 9
# assert.metric.semantic.callsites: 11
# assert.metric.call_edges.count: 11
# oracle: self
# oracle.stamp: 8d23832614e4e686
#---
#
# `ap/2` is specialised for each member of the capture's union: one body reads
# the capture as a raw float, the other as an integer. The closure was built
# over `int | float`, so its capture slot is a tagged word, and reading it as a
# raw float is correct only for a closure that holds a float. The arm's test
# reads the held value's kind first, so neither arm runs on the wrong one.
defmodule Main do
  def ap(f, x), do: f.(x)

  def run(flag) do
    default = if flag, do: 1, else: 2.5
    ap(fn k -> default + k end, 10)
  end

  def main(), do: IO.inspect({run(true), run(false)})
end

Main.main()
